      "side": 1,
      "message": "I didn\u0027t think of it on the prior CL, and src/sksl uses a mix of both std::vector and skia_private::TArray\u003c\u003e so the specific choice isn\u0027t critical.  Our code is an awkward mix of TArray from before, then thinking we could use std::vector and then realizing it tended to be higher code size and worse performance than TArray so have switched back in new code, but haven\u0027t gone through and purged the std::vector usage.\n\nI would think for uint32_t, std::vector will be plenty fast and not make a measurable difference, but if you think it\u0027s easy to swap out and re-measure perf, could be nice to compare to TArray.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
