      "writtenOn": "2025-06-18T16:21:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gave it a try, it was a small change. But with TArray I see a consistent 8~10% regression compared with vector. Didn\u0027t dive into it, but looking at TArray while trying to make the change, I suspect it\u0027s because it doesn\u0027t have faster paths for basic types; like memcpy instead of loop and placement new, that sort of thing.\n\nTArray would be a regression compared with OutputStream, so I\u0027d say let\u0027s keep std::vector? If TArray is used so commonly, perhaps it merits some further independent investigation.\n\nFor future reference:\n\n- To measure SPIR-V gen perf: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1009736\n- Using TArray: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1009737",
      "parentUuid": "c61ee97a_5d97f028",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
