      "writtenOn": "2025-06-18T17:15:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interesting, I agree lets keep std::vector for now.  There could be a difference in allocation policy that is impacting things. Assuming TArray is inferring the `MEM_MOVE\u003dtrue` parameter correctly for a uint32_t, it should be using memcpy for growing the storage and for the `move_back` calls.  It does use placement new for a single push_back, so maybe that is not getting quite as simple of an instruction as memcpy\u0027ing the int directly to the storage.\n\nThanks for testing. I\u0027ll keep this in mind when we do a push to remove STL collections more thoroughly.",
